Id: aud002w
Severity: WARN
Category: logging
Check: check_audit
References: audit.rules(7), augenrules(8)

auditd is running, but no audit rules are loaded ('auditctl -l' says
"No rules"), so it records little beyond what the kernel and PAM send
it anyway. Rules say what to watch.

To fix it, put rules in /etc/audit/rules.d/ and load them with
'augenrules --load'. The audit package ships examples (under
/usr/share/doc/audit*/rules/ or /usr/share/audit/sample-rules/): a
sound start watches /etc/passwd, /etc/shadow, /etc/group, /etc/sudoers
and /etc/sudoers.d for writes, records program execution by root, and
ends with -e 2 so the rules cannot be changed without a reboot.
